A||||4||montage||88 upper control arm shaft, Help!!||||1||
Z||000000||montage||07-12-2001||06:55 AM||||I decided to rebuild the front end and everything was going well until I got to the upper control arm shaft. On the driver side one of the mounting bolts won't come off. I've heated it with a propane torch (in the process of setting up real torches for my shop by this weekend) and PB blasted it for a week. The head is getting striped but I can pound a 9/16 on it yet and still torque it. Well I got it to move but what happened is I unscrewed the other bolt too far and the plate under the crossmember with the nuts welded to it turned and bent. So I called a used parts dealer and he told me that plate is welded to the crossmember. I just don't see how it could be welded to the crossmember how else would you do adjustments for alignment? Any insight to how this plate is mounted? Thanks, I sure miss my wheels!||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||07-12-2001||09:00 AM||||The nuts are welded to a small plate theat connects the two nuts. The plate is not welded to the crossmember so you don't have to worry about that.  When the two bolts are removed that nut plate falls off.  In a worse case senerio you would have to grind the head of the bolt off or burn it off with a torch. I found it is best to leave both bolts in the plate till both are loose.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||montage||07-12-2001||01:41 PM||||Thanks skitime I finally convinced the used parts dealer that the plate was not welded.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||07-12-2001||09:11 PM||||Use a nut splitter.||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||07-12-2001||09:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>Use a nut splitter.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Unfortunately you can't get to the nut which actually the whole problem. I don't think it would work on the head of a bolt.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
